# What goes in the SDIST — deliberately NOT the wheel.
#
# The wheel is code only: `tests/test_packaging_contents.py` asserts it contains zero
# non-.py entries outside dist-info. MANIFEST.in cannot add files to a wheel
# built by setuptools without `include_package_data`, which is exactly why it is the right
# tool here — it makes the source distribution complete (a contributor can `pip download
# --no-binary` and get a runnable checkout with the suites and the test suite) while
# leaving the installed program untouched.
graft examples
graft docs
graft tests
include data/models.json
include CONTRIBUTING.md CHANGELOG.md SECURITY.md CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
include action.yml
prune ops
prune .claude
prune reports
global-exclude *.pyc __pycache__/*
